Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wcn36xx: supply a valid PHY address without DT MAC data

A zero PHY address makes newly created monitor netdevs unusable. Preserve
valid board-supplied addresses; otherwise provide a local unicast fallback.
The board-specific userspace .link still applies the saved station address.


---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/main.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/main.c
@@ -1637,6 +1637,14 @@
 		SET_IEEE80211_PERM_ADDR(wcn->hw, addr);
 	}
 
+	if (!is_valid_ether_addr(wcn->hw->wiphy->perm_addr)) {
+		u8 fallback[ETH_ALEN];
+
+		eth_random_addr(fallback);
+		SET_IEEE80211_PERM_ADDR(wcn->hw, fallback);
+		wcn36xx_warn("No valid DT MAC address, using a local random address\n");
+	}
+
 	ret = wcn36xx_platform_get_resources(wcn, pdev);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_destroy_ept;
